  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pepsico India Holding Pvt. Ltd. vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 21 November, 2019 Author: Vishal Dhagat Bench: Vishal Dhagat 1 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc-5233-2018 (Pepsico India Holding Pvt. Ltd. Vs The State Of Madhya 12 Jabalpur, Dated : 21-11-2019 Shri Surendra Singh, senior counsel with Shri Abhisekh Arja Advocate for the petitioner.",
    "facts": "Shri Rohit Sohgaura, learned Govt. Advocate for the respond Complainant, Food Inspector, has filed complaint under Sections 2, 7 and 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. On 05.12.2009 Food Inspector purchased packets of product Kurkure along with other food articles. Packet was send for examination at State Food Laboratory. Public Analyst examined the product on 30.12.2009 and submitted report on 11.01.2010. Manufacturing date of product was 21.11.2009 and product was best before 4 months i.e. till 20.03.2010. Visible extraneous matter present and product Kurkure Masala Munch was found to be adulterated. Deputy Director, Food and Drug Administration gave sanction for prosecution on 21.02.2011. Notice to petitioner company was issued on 28.10.2010 under Section 14 (A) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. It is submitted by learned Senior Counsel appearing for petitioner that product has crossed its shelf life of 4 months i.e. 20.03.2010 and the same could not be send for re-analysis and notices were received after its best before date. Thus, there is denial of right of re-analysis which is fatal to the prosecution case. It is clear that complaint was filed after shelf life of the product and valuable rights of 2 MCRC-5233-2018 petitioner under Section 13 (2) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 is violated.",
